WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.660
Hi, I'm Phil from BBC Learning English.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.760
Today I'm going to tell you how to use make and do.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.260
Now, they can be tricky and there are some exceptions.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.800
But here are four things to remember.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.520
We use make when we create something...

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.640
like this cake!

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.160
We use do to talk about an activity.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.140
What are you doing?

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.480
I'm doing some work.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.240
We can use make to talk about something that

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.900
causes a reaction.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.340
This music really makes me want to sing!

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.760
We can also use do with general activities.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.320
What are you doing tomorrow?

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.520
I'm not doing anything.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.980
Have you got any plans?

